### Rule 1: Never Format Locale-Sensitive Values Directly

Application code must not call `Date.toLocaleDateString()`, `Intl.DateTimeFormat()`, `toLocaleString()`, or any formatting API directly. All formatting must go through the `locale` concern in `mmes-common-core`.

**Wrong:**
```typescript
// ❌ Direct formatting — locale not controlled by platform
const display = date.toLocaleDateString('en-US');
const amount = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' }).format(1234.56);
```

**Right:**
```typescript
// ✅ Platform-controlled formatting
import { formatDate, formatCurrency } from '@mmes/core/locale';

const display = formatDate(date, locale, 'short');
const amount = formatCurrency(1234.56, locale, 'USD');
```

